From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Spindler <richard@lateralblast.com.au>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 37/55] sshconnect: name the port in the connect failure
 message

ssh_connect_direct() printed "ssh: connect to host H port %s: reason" with
strport, which only the loop over addresses fills in. With HappyEyes yes that
loop does not run, so every failure said "port : reason". Print the port that
was asked for.
---
 sshconnect.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sshconnect.c b/sshconnect.c
index 9163f1808..989d4ad18 100644
--- a/sshconnect.c
+++ b/sshconnect.c
@@ -601,8 +601,9 @@ ssh_connect_direct(struct ssh *ssh, const char *host, struct addrinfo *aitop,
 
 	/* Return failure if we didn't get a successful connection. */
 	if (sock == -1) {
-		error("ssh: connect to host %s port %s: %s",
-		    host, strport, errno == 0 ? "failure" : strerror(errno));
+		/* strport is only set by the loop above, not by happy eyeballs */
+		error("ssh: connect to host %s port %d: %s",
+		    host, (int)port, errno == 0 ? "failure" : strerror(errno));
 		return -1;
 	}
 
